<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Mar industry output rises 0.5 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Mar industry output rises 0.5 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT  Mar 97     Feb 97	Mar 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +0.5	 +2.0(+1.9) +2.7</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +4.7	 +7.0(+7.1) -3.4</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     100.4	 99.9(100.0)95.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. Previously announced data in parentheses.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    Mar 97		   Feb 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			70.8	-2.5	72.6	-1.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    99.7	+0.2	99.5	+1.2</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   104.1	+0.1     104.0	+3.1</p>
<p>	Capital goods	96.2	-2.7	98.9	-0.6</p>
<p>	Consumer durables  91.6	+6.5	86.0	+0.9</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    100.1	+3.4	96.8	-0.3</p>
<p> Energy output	    102.7	+2.1     100.6	-8.1</p>
<p> Construction	     113.4	+2.8     110.3     +17.6</p>
<p>Two month comparison Mar/Feb 1997 with Dec 1996-Jan 1997:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +1.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  +2.0</p>
<p> Construction			    +3.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -0.5</p>
<p> Mining				    -5.0</p>
<p> Energy output			   -6.0</p>
<p> Consumer durables and goods	 +3.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +3.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Mar-Feb 97 with Mar-Feb 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +3.3</p>
<p> Mining				    -7.8</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +2.8</p>
<p>  Incl: Intermediate goods	   +5.5</p>
<p>	  Capital goods		  +1.2</p>
<p>	  Consumer durables	    unch</p>
<p>	  Consumer goods		 unch</p>
<p> Energy output			   -3.6</p>
<p> Construction			   +16.9</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
</text>
